  "output": "The analysis is complete. This is a very early-stage Next.js app (landing page + get-started + sign-in/up + a single `/sources` console page), so most classic performance anti-patterns simply don't have surface area yet. Here's the breakdown:\n\n## 1. N+1 Query Patterns\n**None found.** The only data-access code, `lib/server/sources.ts`, does a single `db.select().from(sources)`. No API routes or server actions exist yet to loop-and-query.\n\n## 2. Unnecessary React Re-renders\n**None found.** No Context providers, no `React.memo`, no unmemoized-value pitfalls. All `\"use client\"` boundaries are justified (Framer Motion animations, `usePathname()`, Clerk hooks) — nothing should be a server component that isn't.\n\n## 3. Caching Opportunities — 1 real finding\n`lib/server/sources.ts:23-30`:\n```ts\nexport async function countSourcesBySide() {\n  const all = await listSources();   // separate DB round trip\n  ...\n}\n```\nThis function is currently unused, but it duplicates the query in `listSources()`. As soon as a page calls both `listSources()` and `countSourcesBySide()` in the same request, you get two round trips for identical data with no dedup.\n\n**Fix — wrap `listSources` in React's `cache()`:**\n```ts\nimport { cache } from \"react\";\n\nexport const listSources = cache(async (): Promise<Source[]> => {\n  return db.select().from(sources);\n});\n```\n`cache()` dedupes calls within a single request/render pass, so `countSourcesBySide()` calling `listSources()` internally becomes free once the outer page has already called it.\n\n## 4. Memory Leaks\n**None found.** Zero `useEffect` hooks anywhere in the app code, so no subscriptions/timers/listeners to leak. No Supabase realtime code exists yet. The Postgres client in `lib/db/index.ts` is correctly cached on `globalThis` to survive HMR — a bounded singleton, not a leak.\n\n## 5. Redundant Computations\nMinor, low-stakes: `countSourcesBySide()` (same function as above) does three separate `.filter()` passes over the same array where a single reduce would do:\n```ts\n// current: 3 passes\nconst crm = all.filter(s => SOURCE_KIND_SIDE[s.kind] === \"crm\").length;\nconst warehouse = all.filter(s => SOURCE_KIND_SIDE[s.kind] === \"warehouse\").length;\nconst synthetic = all.filter(s => SOURCE_KIND_SIDE[s.kind] === \"synthetic\").length;\n\n// fix: 1 pass\nconst counts = all.reduce((acc, s) => {\n  const side = SOURCE_KIND_SIDE[s.kind];\n  acc[side] = (acc[side] ?? 0) + 1;\n  return acc;\n}, {} as Record<string, number>);\n```\nTrivial at current data volumes — not worth prioritizing.\n\n**Bottom line:** nothing urgent to fix today. The one actionable change is wrapping `listSources()` in React `cache()` now, before more pages (runs, conflicts, audit — already stubbed in the nav rail) start calling shared data-fetchers and silently duplicating queries.\n",
